meta {
  name: 16 Look up another user's profile (1) for comparison
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/api/users/1/profile
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.id: isDefined
  res.body.role: isDefined
}

docs {
  Note: deliberately no auth — the public profile should be public.

  This is a "what does ANY agent's profile look like" comparison. If user
  id=1 is the admin/seed user, fine — I want to see what fields are
  populated for a longer-tenured user. Especially looking for
  `closedDealCount` / `responseRate` again (post-audit promise).

  If the response 401s, that's a finding: a public profile should be
  reachable when an owner is comparing agents before signup.
}
